cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TEFAR in your work, please cite the preprint below (preferred-citation). To cite the software itself, use the Zenodo DOI."
type: software
title: "TEFAR: TMS-EEG / EEG FieldTrip Artefact Removal"
abstract: >-
  A lightweight, configurable MATLAB framework for semi-automatic
  artefact-component classification in EEG and TMS-EEG, built on
  FieldTrip. A core function detects line noise, blinks, lateral eye
  movements, cranial muscle, cardiac activity, and the TMS decay and
  recharge artefacts from established independent-component
  signatures, using robust (median/MAD) thresholds, and suggests
  components for removal; the researcher confirms them by visual
  inspection.
